      "updated_at": "2018-05-21T14:21:43Z",
      "body": "@daniellemoorhead there is something I don't understand here, when you say\r\n\r\n> To ensure that the enterprise can see the full order history for one email address (user), but protect the previous owner of the email address.\r\n\r\nI understand your design proposal but sightly disagree. I see your arguments to say that a guest user -\r\n- might have misspelt the email address used\r\n- or might have used an email, then close his mailbox and then someone else might have open the same email address (I'm not sure that's authorized by email providers though so not sure about that argument)\r\n- a customer might have used a random email and then it happens that the real people using that email creates an account\r\n\r\n**BUT here are my objections:**\r\n- If a guest user uses an email that happens to exist (point 3) the real user would have received an order confirmation email and would have write to us saying \"I never ordered, how did you get my email, etc.\" So for me this can't happen, or if it does it woud be a mistake and we would treat it as a mistake.\r\n- If a guest user misspelt her email (point 1) and this misspelt address happens to be a real one and the real user creates an account, we are in the same case as just described. Else there is no issue, she just didn't receive her previous order confirmations, and she wouldn't see when registering the orders made through that error email.\r\n- Point 2 I think is impossibe, I checked and gmail for instance doesn't authorize to create an email address already used by someone else before even if this user has closed it (https://support.google.com/mail/answer/56256?hl=en&visit_id=1-636625089850149575-3195862716&rd=1) so this case for me can't happen.\r\n\r\nSo for me: \"The guest order history does not show in the registered user's order history.\"  > I disagree, as a new registered user I want to see in my account the past orders I made with that same email address when I was still a guest and had no account.\r\n\r\n**So I would simplify that story and just say that:**\r\n- the previous guest records are associated with the new register user\r\n- so manager see all info attached to user\r\n- user see all info in his account\r\n\r\nDo you agree @daniellemoorhead ?\r\n\r\n",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
