      "updated_at": "2018-05-23T12:35:08Z",
      "body": "Ok I get your points @mkllnk \r\nThen my question is: can we just consider that all the records from before the account is created remain as guest and are not connected to the new account at all? Is it really a problem for the hub manager if she doesn't see the records associated to that customer? I mean the problems you mention on the user side will be the same on the hub manager side, if the email was used by someone esle the hub manager will see a wrong record associated to a customer.\r\n**SO my proposal is: we don't associate any guest record to new accounts.** And we close this issue :-)\r\nThe hub manager will still see the past orders but they will not be associated with the account of the new user. I don't think it's really a problem, if the hub manager filter orders with the email she will see all the orders anyway, so why would she need to have the guest orders formally associated with the customer? ",
