      "created_at": "2018-05-25T12:25:53Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-05-25T17:21:53Z",
      "body": "> The only question I have is about the impact of this on the customer list for the enterprise - will the same email address show up twice, and thus be duplicated if the enterprise emails their customers? And even if this does happen, does it matter? And can enterprises even email their entire customer list?\r\n\r\nFor the enterprise, what will happen is that for one given email, the hub will see that:\r\n![screenshot from 2018-05-25 14-11-09](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8135376/40543643-8b2fefae-6025-11e8-85ed-37cc4b8d08a6.png)\r\nWhich I agree is not so good... Can't we technically \"deactivate\"/\"archive\" the old email (so that it doesn't appear in the  cutomer list and the hub only see the account now that it is created?) But then in case the email is a mistake (one of the three cases above) we would archive an entry that is valid?\r\n\r\nActually I think the only solution to really solve that problem would be to force users to create themselves an account in order to be able to shop :-o \r\n\r\nProbably that's why all websites went in that direction.\r\nDo we want to do that?\r\nElse we need to decide:\r\n- either to accept the risk of reconciliation errors (low) and merge guest records into new user account\r\n- either to accept that there is this strange duplicate in the hub manager \"customer\" view... \r\n\r\n@sstead what do you think? and @sauloperez ? @lin-d-hop ",
